//! GridCraft on phones: the engine as a native library for the Android app in `android/`, with
//! bindings generated by [UniFFI](https://mozilla.github.io/uniffi-rs).
//!
//! The phone UI is one more frontend next to the desktop app, the CLI/MCP server and the web
//! build. Every edit is an engine command run by id ([`MobileSession::execute`]), so undo and the
//! never-crash guard behave as they do on the desktop. The app draws the grid itself from a
//! [`Viewport`]: the visible rows and columns and, for each cell there, what it shows and how.
//!
//! Sizes and positions are in sheet units (96-dpi pixels, as in the file), from the sheet's top
//! left corner. Colours are ARGB in an `i32` (what an Android colour int holds).
//!
//! Threading: every method may be called from any thread. The session lock is held only to run a
//! command or take a snapshot of the workbook (shared, so the copy is cheap); viewports are built
//! from the snapshot after releasing it.
#![forbid(unsafe_code)]
#![deny(clippy::unwrap_used, clippy::expect_used, clippy::panic, clippy::unimplemented, clippy::todo, clippy::unreachable)]

use std::sync::{Arc, Mutex, MutexGuard, PoisonError};

